# aurora.local / packages/core/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/core/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here instead, where they survive in git and can be reviewed/updated
# like any other file. Copy or merge into packages/core/pins.env to adopt.
#
# See dev/notes/pinnable-versions-progress.md for the full inventory and
# reasoning behind every choice in this file.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run, so
# compose.yml still says `image: caddy:2-alpine` etc. compose.yml is
# untouched by this work; this file is the curated data, ready for that
# step when the owner chooses it.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest — tag kept for human readability, digest
# recorded because a tag can be re-pointed and a digest cannot. Note this
# differs from scripts/pin.sh --refresh, which currently discards the tag
# (see progress log finding #2); that script would need a small change to
# agree with this file's format before being run against it.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# caddy — official Docker Hub image. Caddy's own docs recommend the floating
# `2` / `2-alpine` tag for automatic patch updates, but that is exactly the
# moving pointer the unpinned-image-tags security rule flags. Pinned instead
# to the version `2-alpine` currently resolves to: 2.11.4-alpine (built
# 2026-06-22, ~8 weeks old, stable — not an rc/beta). Multi-arch: linux/amd64,
# linux/arm/v6, linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64/v8, linux/ppc64le, linux/riscv64,
# linux/s390x — confirmed via `docker buildx imagetools inspect`; covers both
# the Optiplex (amd64) and a Pi (arm64). Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_CADDY=caddy:2.11.4-alpine@sha256:5f5c8640aae01df9654968d946d8f1a56c497f1dd5c5cda4cf95ab7c14d58648

# authelia/authelia — part of core (SSO always-on). Latest stable release is
# 4.39.20, released 2026-05-26 (confirmed against the project's GitHub
# releases page; not an rc/beta). Verified the tag `4.39.20` resolves to the
# same manifest-list digest as `:latest`. Multi-arch: linux/amd64,
# linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64 — covers both the Optiplex (amd64) and a Pi
# (arm64). Checked 2026-08-15. Migrated from packages/identity 2026-08-25.
IMAGE_AUTHELIA=authelia/authelia:4.39.20@sha256:1b363e9279e742397966333f364e0876ae02bf5c876de73e83af6d48c57ff51b
